.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-s3-events-add - Add an event webhook to a bucket


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro s3 events add   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add an event webhook to a bucket

.PP
\fBBucket events\fP send a signed HTTPS POST to your address when an object is created (upload, copy, multipart upload), deleted, or a bulk delete runs. Body: \fB{"id", "event", "created_at", "data": {service_id, bucket, key, size, etag, content_type, version_id (Protected Storage), method (put / multipart / delete / bulk), source (api / panel), access_key_id, event_time}}\fR - no object content. Headers: \fBX-Gyro-Event\fR, \fBX-Gyro-Delivery\fR (unique id, use it to drop duplicates), \fBX-Gyro-Timestamp\fR, \fBX-Gyro-Signature: sha256=HMAC-SHA256(secret, timestamp + "." + raw body)\fR (same format as account webhooks). Delivery is at least once with no ordering guarantee; a non-2xx answer or no answer within 6 s is retried (8 attempts, about 2 hours); 20 failures in a row disable the webhook (\fBdisabled_reason\fR = \fBauto_failures\fR). Requests come from 45.87.174.151, 45.87.174.153, 45.87.174.154. Targets: https only, port 443 or 8443, public internet (private, loopback and Gyro platform addresses are refused, the name is resolved again on every delivery). Filters: \fBprefix\fR (key starts with) and \fBsuffix\fR (key ends with one of, at most 10). Limits: 5 webhooks per bucket, 20 per service (\fBs3.max_event_hooks\fR, raised with a support ticket). Price: a monthly free allowance per bucket (see \fBGET /cloud/storage/{id}/events/usage\fR) plus prepaid event packs valid in the month of purchase; no overage invoice: when the allowance is used up new events are not sent. Known gaps: a bulk delete does not list the keys; lifecycle deletions produce no event. The answer carries \fBsecret\fR once. A refusal is 422 \fBtool_action_failed\fR with a message in the account language (invalid / private / unresolvable URL, port, event type, limits).

.PP
API: POST /cloud/storage/{id}/buckets/{bucket}/events (operationId createBucketEventWebhook, scope services_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--description\fP=""
	description

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB--events\fP=[]
	default: all three. Short names created / deleted / deleted_bulk are accepted

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--prefix\fP=""
	prefix

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--suffix\fP=[]
	a comma separated text is accepted too

.PP
\fB--url\fP=""
	url


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--account\fP=""
	act in another account you are a panel user of (id from \fBgyro account list\fR; "self" = your own; env GYRO_ACCOUNT, profile default: \fBgyro account use\fR)

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only ids

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0s
	overall timeout, e.g. 30s, 10m

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	show all table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	do not ask for confirmation


